# Search certificates (generated)

Generated by `tools/radix-circuit-search --lean` (`--max 512`). For every length
`2 ≤ N ≤ 512` the search's best plan is checked by Corollary 37 (`Plan.certify`):
its validity, length and cost are evaluated by the kernel (`decide +kernel`), so the
reported gate count is a theorem — an exact Fourier circuit of that size exists.
Do not edit by hand; regenerate with the tool.
-/

